# Generated image data (the full 30-pair dataset -- kept out of git,
# ~130MB total, regenerable via `python3 generate_dataset.py`).
#
# EXCEPTION: the 5 curated pairs the deployed web app actually serves
# (webapp/backend/examples.py::CURATED) are explicitly un-ignored below.
# They were previously added with `git add -f`, which works but is a trap:
# a future `git add outputs/` looks like it should pick up any new/changed
# curated pair but silently won't, because the broad *.png rule above still
# wins for anything not explicitly negated. Listing them here means the
# curated set is self-maintaining and the exception is visible in the one
# place someone would think to look, instead of only living in shell
# history. If you add a new curated example to examples.py, add its two
# PNGs here too.
outputs/reference/*.png
outputs/search/*.png
!outputs/reference/dram_002_ref.png
!outputs/reference/dram_018_ref.png
!outputs/reference/dram_020_ref.png
!outputs/reference/finfet_005_ref.png
!outputs/reference/finfet_009_ref.png
!outputs/search/dram_002_search.png
!outputs/search/dram_018_search.png
!outputs/search/dram_020_search.png
!outputs/search/finfet_005_search.png
!outputs/search/finfet_009_search.png

# Generated datasets / large local artifacts
outputs/generated/
dataset/generated/

